Where does the keydown listener need to live for CTRL-K? I need to activate it from whereever, so it needs some broader context.
I think I will add a wrapper div for the entire App and add that listener there. Wait, I can't add it to that div or the root element (here with an id 'app' as seen in main.ts) as both are descendants of body, and the event would bubble up. Bubbling travels upwards through ancestors of whatever's focused. If I add that listener to body it would bubble up. The real choice is adding it to either document or window. Document is the more "conventional" choice here.
